-- title:
--   Degree-zero principal divisors on K(j,j_N)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $N$ a nonzero natural number. Write $j_q \in K((q))$ for `jqModC K`, the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot \big(E_4^3\,\eta^{-24}\big)$ obtained from the integral power series `jNum` $=$ `eisenstein4`$^3\cdot$`dedekindEtaUnitInv` by coefficientwise reduction to $K$ and multiplication by the monomial $q^{-1}$; and write $j_{q^N}$ for `jqNModC K N`, the image of $j_q$ under the ring endomorphism `qExpand K N` of $K((q))$ that multiplies all exponents by $N$ (substitution $q \mapsto q^N$). The hypothesis is that $j_{q^N}$ is separable over the $K$-intermediate field $K(j_q)$ of $K((q))$ generated by $j_q$, i.e. its minimal polynomial over that field is separable. The conclusion is `HasPrincipalDivisors K F` for $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, the $K$-intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated by $\{j_q, j_{q^N}\}$: for every $f \in F$ with $f \neq 0$ there is a finitely supported function $D$ from the places of $F$ over $K$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $\operatorname{image}(K)$, distinct from $F$ itself, and principal ideal rings) to $\mathbb{Z}$ such that $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ for every such place $v$, and $\sum_v D(v)\cdot \deg v = 0$.
--
--   This is the product formula, or degree-zero property of principal divisors, for the function field $K(j, j_N)$ of the modular curve $X_0(N)$ over $K$, realised concretely inside the field of Laurent series in $q$; the separability hypothesis on $j_{q^N}$ over $K(j_q)$ makes the statement available in arbitrary characteristic once it is checked. It is used in the analysis of the reduction of places of this function field, in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.red_surjective_of_level`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.red_surjective_of_level).
